  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday night through next Thursday)\nIssued at 1225 PM CDT Fri Jul 31 2026\n\nThe overall theme for Sunday and beyond is hotter and drier \nunderneath the eastern portion of an upper high - the center of\nwhich is poised to hold over the Desert Southwest most days\nkeeping the worst of the heat well to our west. There is more \nevidence for weakening of the height fields locally as early as \nTuesday thanks to a robust upper low and trough careening from the\nGulf of Alaska through the Dakotas. This feature could subject \nour northern zones to some disturbances or even nocturnal precip\nchances in WNW flow, although this is a low potential and not \nreflected well by ensembles or the NBM at this time. What is \nhigher confidence is the return of triple-digit highs, mainly off\nthe Caprock, with some opportunities for more Heat Advisories.",
